"""Local-only live geographic connection view and legacy history visibility hooks."""

LIVE_GLOBE_HTML = r'''
<section id="live-globe" class="live-globe" aria-labelledby="live-globe-title">
  <header class="live-globe-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">LIVE CONNECTION ATLAS</p><h3 id="live-globe-title" tabindex="-1">Your PC and the wider network</h3><p>Observed packet directions, placed with approximate IP locations.</p></div><span id="live-globe-status" class="live-globe-badge">Checking local capture</span></header>
  <div class="live-monitor-controls"><button id="live-background-start" type="button" disabled>Enable background monitoring</button><button id="live-background-stop" type="button" disabled>Stop monitoring</button><button id="live-interface-change" type="button">Choose interface</button><span id="live-interface-name">Reading saved interface…</span></div>
  <p id="live-background-status" class="live-globe-note">Checking saved monitoring settings…</p><p id="live-action-status" class="live-action-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></p><button id="live-action-retry" type="button" hidden>Retry local controls</button>
  <div class="live-globe-layout">
    <div class="live-atlas"><div id="live-globe-stage" class="live-globe-stage"><canvas id="live-land" width="640" height="560" aria-hidden="true"></canvas><canvas id="live-flows" width="640" height="560" role="img" aria-label="Geographic reference; live connections are listed alongside it." tabindex="0" aria-describedby="live-motion-status live-camera-status"></canvas><span class="live-globe-map-credit">Natural Earth land · illustrative connection paths</span></div><div class="live-motion-controls"><label class="live-camera-label">View<select id="live-globe-camera"><option value="follow" selected>Follow activity</option><option value="world">World rotation</option><option value="manual">Manual view</option></select></label><label class="live-camera-label live-camera-zoom">Scale<input id="live-globe-zoom" type="range" min="75" max="105" step="1" value="94" aria-label="Globe scale"></label><button type="button" id="live-globe-pause" aria-pressed="false">Pause motion</button><button type="button" id="live-globe-center">Center on internet exit</button><span id="live-motion-status">Drag to turn · arrow keys to rotate</span></div><p id="live-camera-status" class="live-camera-status" role="status">Follow activity · waiting for recent mapped connections.</p><div class="live-direction-key"><span class="live-outbound">→ Outbound</span><span class="live-inbound">← Inbound</span><span class="live-origin-key">◎ Incoming origin</span><span>Other paths · slate</span><span>● Approximate internet exit</span></div><p id="live-origin-status" class="live-globe-note">Incoming origins appear when recent traffic has a mapped source.</p></div>
    <aside class="live-globe-readout" aria-label="Live connection coverage"><p class="eyebrow">LIVE AND RECENTLY RETAINED</p><dl class="live-globe-totals"><div><dt>Recent in tracked data</dt><dd id="live-active-count">—</dd></div><div><dt>Mapped connections</dt><dd id="live-mapped-count">—</dd></div><div><dt>Unmapped connections</dt><dd id="live-unmapped-count">—</dd></div></dl><p id="live-coverage" class="live-globe-note">Coverage is being checked.</p><h4>Your approximate internet exit</h4><p id="live-anchor">Location not loaded.</p><p id="live-precision" class="live-globe-note">IP location describes a network exit, not an exact PC position.</p><button id="live-geography-refresh" type="button" disabled aria-describedby="live-geography-destinations">Update location data</button><button id="live-geography-disable" type="button" disabled aria-describedby="live-geography-destinations">Disable automatic location updates</button><p id="live-geography-opt-in" class="live-globe-note">Checking location-update setting…</p><p id="live-geography-destinations" class="live-globe-note">Downloads the DB-IP database from download.db-ip.com and checks your public internet address with api64.ipify.org. No captured peer addresses are uploaded.</p><p id="live-geography-status" class="live-globe-note">Checking the local location database…</p><p class="live-globe-note">IP location: <a href="https://db-ip.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">DB-IP City Lite</a></p><time id="live-globe-updated" class="live-globe-note">No live snapshot yet.</time><button id="live-globe-retry" type="button" hidden>Retry live connection check</button></aside>
  </div>
  <details class="live-connection-detail"><summary>Connection details <span id="live-connection-count"></span></summary><p class="live-globe-note">Counts accumulate while a connection remains in this bounded live view. TCP / UDP are transport labels; a port does not establish an application protocol.</p><div class="live-connection-table" role="region" aria-label="Recent observed connections" tabindex="0"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Endpoints</th><th scope="col">Transport</th><th scope="col">A → B</th><th scope="col">B → A</th><th scope="col">Last packet</th></tr></thead><tbody id="live-connection-rows"><tr><td colspan="5">Waiting for a live snapshot.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details>
  <details class="live-location-detail"><summary>Location accuracy, animation and coverage</summary><p>Locations come from the local DB-IP City Lite database. Your internet-exit anchor uses your public internet address; a VPN, carrier gateway or proxy can place it away from this PC. Unknown precision is shown as unknown. Location setup downloads the public database from download.db-ip.com and discovers your public internet address through api64.ipify.org. Enabling location setup allows periodic refresh while background monitoring is on. No captured peer address is sent to either service.</p><p>Paths illustrate recently observed connections, not cables, physical origins or measured packet delays. A path appears only while packet evidence in that direction is recent and capture is running. Moving dots indicate the same recent direction evidence; one dot does not represent one packet. Red expanding rings mark approximate sources of recently observed incoming traffic, not attack verdicts or active network probes. Connections at the same mapped location share a ring. Closed, stale or stopped capture produces no paths or moving traffic. Unmapped and private peers stay in the counts and connection list without invented locations.</p><p>Follow activity frames recent mapped exchanges and visits different regions when they cannot fit in one hemisphere. The far side remains hidden; the camera caption reports visible mapped locations. Dragging, arrow keys or changing scale gives you manual camera control. Choose Follow activity to resume, or World rotation to see every longitude. Reduced motion keeps the camera static.</p><p>Up to 512 connections are tracked in bounded memory and up to 128 are returned. Counts cover this cache; they do not represent every connection on the PC. Older connections may be evicted. Recent means packet evidence within 15 seconds while capture runs; it does not mean an operating-system established socket. Rows can remain for 60 seconds after paths disappear. Background monitoring saves your choice and renews bounded capture sessions while the local HUD runs; brief gaps between sessions may occur. Stopping disables automatic resumption.</p><p id="live-location-source" class="live-globe-note"></p></details>
</section>
'''

